/-!
# Covering a quasi-coherent module by its finite type quasi-coherent submodules

Let `F` be a quasi-coherent module on a scheme `X`. Its quasi-coherent submodules of finite type
form a filtered diagram over `F` (`AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject`), and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_iSup_eq_top` says that `F`
is their colimit as soon as their supremum in `Subobject F` is the whole of `F`. What remains of
the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 01PG] is therefore that supremum hypothesis, and this file
reduces it, in two steps, to the extension lemma [Stacks, Tag 01PF].

The first step is pure sheaf theory and is the last sentence of the source's proof: it suffices
that every section of `F` over an affine open lie in some finite type quasi-coherent submodule of
`F`. Indeed the supremum `S = ⨆ G` is a subobject of `F`, so its inclusion is injective, and that
hypothesis says exactly that the inclusion is locally surjective on sections, because the affine
opens form a basis of the topology. A morphism of sheaves of modules which is both is an
isomorphism, and a subobject whose inclusion is an isomorphism is the top subobject.

The second step produces that submodule from 01PF, again as in the source: a section `s` of `F`
over an open `W` is a morphism `𝒪_W ⟶ F|_W`, whose image is a quasi-coherent submodule of `F|_W`
of finite type, generated by `s`; 01PF extends it to a quasi-coherent submodule of `F` of finite
type, whose sections over `W` then contain `s`. Only the affine case of 01PF is used, and only
through the hypothesis `hext` below, which is weaker than 01PF because an affine open is
quasi-compact.

No quasi-compactness or quasi-separatedness of `X` is used anywhere here; those hypotheses of
01PG enter only through 01PF.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.quasiCompact_ι_of_isCompact` — the inclusion of a quasi-compact open of a
  quasi-separated space is a quasi-compact morphism, which is what makes 01PE applicable.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_forall_isAffineOpen` — the
  finite type quasi-coherent submodules of `F` have supremum `⊤` once every section of `F` over
  an affine open lies in one of them.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_forall_isAffineOpen` —
  the same hypothesis makes the canonical cocone a colimit cocone.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_section_of_extension` — the
  extension lemma 01PF on an open `W` puts every section of `F` over `W` inside a finite type
  quasi-coherent submodule of `F`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_extension` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_extension` — the two
  steps composed: 01PF on affine opens gives both assertions.

## Implementation notes

**No `@[stacks 01PG]` attribute is placed.** Every statement here is conditional on a
reformulation of [Stacks, Tag 01PF]; tagging a conditional statement would make the dashboard
read the assertion as formalized. The first assertion of 01PG, that the diagram is filtered, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_isFiltered` and is unconditional.

The hypothesis these statements are conditional on holds: it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_extension` restricted to affine opens.
Discharging it is not done here, because the unconditional 01PG is proved directly along the same
route in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ResolutionsAndBounds/FiniteTypeSubobjectColimit.lean`, and
composing the reduction below with 01PF would give a second copy of the same conclusion. The
declarations here remain the record of the reduction itself — which needs neither
quasi-compactness nor quasi-separatedness of `X` — and of how much weaker a hypothesis it takes.

A section of `F` over `W` is turned into a morphism out of the structure sheaf of `W` through
`SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv`, which is stated in terms of `SheafOfModules.sections`, a compatible
family over all opens of `W` rather than a single section over `⊤`. Since `⊤` is terminal in the
opens of `W`, such a family is determined by its value there; that is `sectionsOfTop` below.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### The open immersion of a quasi-compact open is quasi-compact -/

/-- **The inclusion of a quasi-compact open of a quasi-separated space is a quasi-compact
morphism.** A quasi-compact open of a quasi-separated space is retrocompact, and retrocompactness
of a subset is exactly spectrality of the inclusion of its subtype, which for a morphism of
schemes is quasi-compactness.

This is the hypothesis every application of [Stacks, Tag 01PE] inside [Stacks, Tag 01PF] needs,
and it holds with no Noetherian assumption: `QuasiSeparatedSpace X` — which 01PF, 01PI and 0G41
all carry already — is the only input. It is stated here rather than in a module of its own
because a one-lemma module is a collision waiting to happen. -/
@[ega "0 9.1.6" "special case",
  ega "IV 1.2.7" "b′ ⇒ b (immersion form)",
  sga "3 VIA 2.6.3" "more general",
  sga "3 VIB 3.7" "partial"]
theorem quasiCompact_ι_of_isCompact [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsCompact U.1) :
    QuasiCompact U.ι :=
  quasiCompact_iff_isSpectralMap.mpr
    (IsRetrocompact_iff_isSpectralMap_subtypeVal.mp (hU.isRetrocompact U.2))

/-! ### From sections over affine opens to the supremum -/

/-- The supremum of the finite type quasi-coherent submodules of a quasi-coherent module `F` is
the whole of `F`, provided every section of `F` over an affine open is the image of a section of
one of them.

This is the formal half of the covering assertion behind **[Stacks, Tag 01PG]**; the hypothesis is
its geometric content, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_extension` derives it from
[Stacks, Tag 01PF]. -/
theorem iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_forall_isAffineOpen
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (hsec : ∀ W : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen W → ∀ s : Γ(F, W),
      ∃ (G : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) (z : Γ((G.1 : X.Modules), W)),
        G.1.arrow.app W z = s) :
    (⨆ G : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F, G.1) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  set J := FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F
  set S : Subobject F := ⨆ G : J, G.1
  let T := SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf
  have hqSheaf : Epi (T.map S.arrow) := by
    apply (TopCat.Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi (T.map S.arrow)).1
    rw [TopCat.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff]
    intro U t x hx
    obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, hWU⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset hx
    have hWle : W ≤ U := fun y hy => hWU hy
    obtain ⟨G, z, hz⟩ := hsec W hW (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWle).op t)
    have hle : G.1 ≤ S := le_iSup (fun G : J => G.1) G
    refine ⟨W, hWle, ⟨(Subobject.ofLE G.1 S hle).app W z, ?_⟩, hxW⟩
    have key := congrArg (fun φ => Scheme.Modules.Hom.app φ W) (Subobject.ofLE_arrow hle)
    rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app] at key
    change (Scheme.Modules.Hom.app S.arrow W)
        ((Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (Subobject.ofLE G.1 S hle) W) z) =
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWle).op t
    rw [← hz, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, key]
  have : Epi S.arrow := T.epi_of_epi_map hqSheaf
  have : IsIso S.arrow := isIso_of_mono_of_epi S.arrow
  simpa only [Subobject.mk_arrow] using Subobject.mk_eq_top_of_isIso S.arrow

/-- A quasi-coherent module is the colimit of the diagram of its finite type quasi-coherent
submodules, provided every section over an affine open lies in one of them.

This is the colimit assertion of **[Stacks, Tag 01PG]** with its geometric input isolated as a
hypothesis. -/
def isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_forall_isAffineOpen
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (hsec : ∀ W : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen W → ∀ s : Γ(F, W),
      ∃ (G : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) (z : Γ((G.1 : X.Modules), W)),
        G.1.arrow.app W z = s) :
    IsColimit (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F) :=
  isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_iSup_eq_top F
    (iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_forall_isAffineOpen F hsec)

/-! ### From the extension lemma to sections over affine opens -/

/-- Sections of `M` over an open `W` are sections of `M|_W` over the whole of `W`. -/
private def restrictTopSectionsIso (M : X.Modules) (W : X.Opens) :
    Γ(M.restrict W.ι, ⊤) ≅ Γ(M, W) :=
  M.restrictAppIso W.ι ⊤ ≪≫ M.presheaf.mapIso (eqToIso (by simp)).op

private lemma restrictTopSectionsIso_naturality {M N : X.Modules} (φ : M ⟶ N) (W : X.Opens) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor W.ι).map φ).app ⊤ ≫ (restrictTopSectionsIso N W).hom =
      (restrictTopSectionsIso M W).hom ≫ φ.app W := by
  change φ.app (W.ι ''ᵁ ⊤) ≫ N.presheaf.map _ = M.presheaf.map _ ≫ φ.app W
  exact (φ.mapPresheaf.naturality _).symm

/-- The compatible family of sections of `M` determined by a section over the whole space, which
is terminal among the opens. -/
private def sectionsOfTop (M : X.Modules) (sTop : Γ(M, ⊤)) : M.sections :=
  M.val.sectionsMk (fun U => M.val.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.unop))).op sTop)
    (by
      intro U V f
      change M.val.presheaf.map f
        (M.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.unop))).op sTop) = _
      exact (M.val.presheaf.map_comp_apply _ f sTop).symm.trans
        (congrArg (fun j => M.val.presheaf.map j sTop) (Subsingleton.elim _ _)))

private lemma sectionsOfTop_top (M : X.Modules) (sTop : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    (sectionsOfTop M sTop).val (op ⊤) = sTop := by
  change M.val.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := (⊤ : X.Opens)))).op sTop = sTop
  rw [show (homOfLE (le_top (a := (⊤ : X.Opens)))) = 𝟙 _ from Subsingleton.elim _ _]
  simp only [PresheafOfModules.presheaf_obj_coe, op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id,
    AddCommGrpCat.hom_id]
  rfl

/-- The submodule of `F|_W` generated by a section of `F` over `W`: it is quasi-coherent and of
finite type, being the image of a morphism out of the structure sheaf of `W`, and the section is
recovered from its sections over the whole of `W`. -/
private lemma exists_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_of_section
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (W : X.Opens) (s : Γ(F, W)) :
    ∃ (I : Subobject (F.restrict W.ι)) (_ : (I : W.toScheme.Modules).IsQuasicoherent)
      (_ : (I : W.toScheme.Modules).IsFiniteType) (y : Γ((I : W.toScheme.Modules), ⊤)),
      (restrictTopSectionsIso F W).hom (I.arrow.app ⊤ y) = s := by
  let Fw : W.toScheme.Modules := F.restrict W.ι
  let O : W.toScheme.Modules := SheafOfModules.unit W.toScheme.ringCatSheaf
  have : O.IsQuasicoherent := (unit_isQuasicoherent_and_isFiniteType (X := W.toScheme)).1
  have : O.IsFiniteType := (unit_isQuasicoherent_and_isFiniteType (X := W.toScheme)).2
  let sTop : Γ(Fw, ⊤) := (restrictTopSectionsIso F W).inv s
  let sLoc : Fw.sections := sectionsOfTop Fw sTop
  let f : O ⟶ Fw := Fw.unitHomEquiv.symm sLoc
  let I : Subobject Fw := imageSubobject f
  let g : O ⟶ (I : W.toScheme.Modules) := factorThruImageSubobject f
  let t : (I : W.toScheme.Modules).sections := (I : W.toScheme.Modules).unitHomEquiv g
  refine ⟨I, imageSubobject_isQuasicoherent f, imageSubobject_isFiniteType f,
    t.val (op ⊤), ?_⟩
  have h : I.arrow.app ⊤ (t.val (op ⊤)) = sTop := by
    change (SheafOfModules.sectionsMap I.arrow t).val (op ⊤) = sTop
    rw [← SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv_comp_apply g I.arrow]
    refine (congrArg (fun φ : O ⟶ Fw => (Fw.unitHomEquiv φ).val (op ⊤))
      (imageSubobject_arrow_comp f)).trans ?_
    exact (congrArg (fun z : Fw.sections => z.val (op ⊤))
      (Fw.unitHomEquiv.apply_symm_apply sLoc)).trans (sectionsOfTop_top Fw sTop)
  rw [h]
  exact (restrictTopSectionsIso F W).inv_hom_id_apply s

/-- **The second step.** If every finite type quasi-coherent submodule of `F|_W` extends to a
finite type quasi-coherent submodule of `F` — which is **[Stacks, Tag 01PF]** for the open `W` —
then every section of `F` over `W` is the image of a section of a finite type quasi-coherent
submodule of `F`. -/
theorem exists_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_section_of_extension
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (W : X.Opens) (s : Γ(F, W))
    (hext : ∀ G : Subobject (F.restrict W.ι),
      (G : W.toScheme.Modules).IsQuasicoherent → (G : W.toScheme.Modules).IsFiniteType →
      ∃ G' : Subobject F, (G' : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (G' : X.Modules).IsFiniteType ∧
        ∃ e : (G' : X.Modules).restrict W.ι ≅ (G : W.toScheme.Modules),
          (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor W.ι).map G'.arrow = e.hom ≫ G.arrow) :
    ∃ (G : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F) (z : Γ((G.1 : X.Modules), W)),
      G.1.arrow.app W z = s := by
  obtain ⟨I, hIqc, hIft, y, hy⟩ := exists_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_of_section F W s
  obtain ⟨G', hG'qc, hG'ft, e, he⟩ := hext I hIqc hIft
  refine ⟨⟨G', hG'qc, hG'ft⟩,
    (restrictTopSectionsIso (G' : X.Modules) W).hom (e.inv.app ⊤ y), ?_⟩
  have hnat := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (restrictTopSectionsIso_naturality (G'.arrow) W) (e.inv.app ⊤ y)
  rw [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] at hnat
  have hid : Scheme.Modules.Hom.app e.hom ⊤ (Scheme.Modules.Hom.app e.inv ⊤ y) = y := by
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app, e.inv_hom_id]
    simp
  rwa [← hnat, he, Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hid]

/-! ### The two steps composed -/

/-- The supremum of the finite type quasi-coherent submodules of a quasi-coherent module `F` is
the whole of `F`, granted the extension lemma **[Stacks, Tag 01PF]** on affine opens. -/
theorem iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_extension
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (hext : ∀ W : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen W → ∀ G : Subobject (F.restrict W.ι),
      (G : W.toScheme.Modules).IsQuasicoherent → (G : W.toScheme.Modules).IsFiniteType →
      ∃ G' : Subobject F, (G' : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (G' : X.Modules).IsFiniteType ∧
        ∃ e : (G' : X.Modules).restrict W.ι ≅ (G : W.toScheme.Modules),
          (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor W.ι).map G'.arrow = e.hom ≫ G.arrow) :
    (⨆ G : FiniteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject F, G.1) = ⊤ :=
  iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_forall_isAffineOpen F
    fun W hW s => exists_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_section_of_extension F W s (hext W hW)

/-- **The colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 01PG], granted [Stacks, Tag 01PF] on affine opens.**
A quasi-coherent module is the colimit of the diagram of its quasi-coherent submodules of finite
type.

This is the whole of the reduction of 01PG to 01PF. The hypothesis is weaker than 01PF: it asks
for the extension only across affine opens, which are quasi-compact. -/
def isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_extension
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (hext : ∀ W : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen W → ∀ G : Subobject (F.restrict W.ι),
      (G : W.toScheme.Modules).IsQuasicoherent → (G : W.toScheme.Modules).IsFiniteType →
      ∃ G' : Subobject F, (G' : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (G' : X.Modules).IsFiniteType ∧
        ∃ e : (G' : X.Modules).restrict W.ι ≅ (G : W.toScheme.Modules),
          (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor W.ι).map G'.arrow = e.hom ≫ G.arrow) :
    IsColimit (finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F) :=
  isColimit_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone_of_iSup_eq_top F
    (iSup_finiteTypeQuasicoherentSubobject_eq_top_of_extension F hext)

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
